WEBVTT

00:02.409 --> 00:03.876
Legend has it that...

00:05.045 --> 00:07.843
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:08.181 --> 00:13.517
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.988 --> 00:20.153
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.273 --> 00:40.702
<i>The Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.980 --> 00:46.816
<i>Rushing through my innocent
youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.355 --> 00:54.260
<i>This soul of mine is
so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.929 --> 00:59.695
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.799 --> 01:02.996
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.773 --> 01:13.838
<i>This is what I'm wishing
for as I sing this song.</i>

01:14.013 --> 01:19.849
<i>I want you to acknowledge
me, that's all.</i>

01:20.720 --> 01:27.990
<i>You smiled at me for
the very first time.</i>

01:28.161 --> 01:36.569
<i>Thank you so much, thank you
from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.270 --> 01:38.931
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.681 --> 01:52.117
<i>Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:54.788 --> 02:00.351
With Ryoma Sakamoto's help, the
Choshu forces took control...

02:00.493 --> 02:04.862
...of several key Bakufu
holdings in northern Kyushu.

02:11.271 --> 02:15.731
The Choshu forces next set their
sights on the fall of Kokura, but...

02:15.875 --> 02:20.209
...the defense was formidable; Takasugi
and his men faced an uphill battle.

02:20.413 --> 02:25.282
Meanwhile, the Bakufu forces
assembled a vast fleet in Kokura Bay.

02:30.890 --> 02:34.690
So that's the Bakufu fleet's
flagship, the Fujiyamaru...

02:35.161 --> 02:36.287
It's huge!

02:37.197 --> 02:38.755
I have sighted nine ships...

02:38.898 --> 02:40.263
The flagship is the Fujiyamamaru!

02:40.967 --> 02:42.559
Report to Commander Takasugi at
once!

02:42.669 --> 02:43.397
Yes, sir!

02:45.672 --> 02:51.269
<i>Battle in the Darkness</i>

02:52.912 --> 02:54.504
What should we do?

02:54.848 --> 02:57.408
Their guard is up on both
land and at sea.

02:57.517 --> 02:59.644
We have no chance of approaching
Kokura.

02:59.819 --> 03:01.252
It's a headache...

03:14.300 --> 03:16.029
Hey, this is just a fight.

03:16.669 --> 03:19.604
First of all, we've got to
beat back that monster ship.

03:19.739 --> 03:24.108
We'll get the most for our money
if we kick them where it counts!

03:26.679 --> 03:31.082
We'll strike before dawn, while it's
still dark. They won't see us coming!

03:31.818 --> 03:33.251
The Deshimura Battery...

03:33.386 --> 03:37.447
Takasugi's troops will
bombard Kokura from here.

03:40.093 --> 03:42.653
At that distance, they're not
likely to hit their targets...

03:43.396 --> 03:45.227
It doesn't matter if they miss.

03:45.431 --> 03:48.093
All they have to do is wake them up.

03:48.401 --> 03:50.562
If they get blasted,
they'll come out for sure.

03:50.870 --> 03:52.861
And that's where I come in!

03:53.239 --> 03:54.501
A night raid, you mean?

03:54.607 --> 03:55.471
That's right.

03:55.742 --> 03:57.676
It's just knocking off
Takasugi's strategy!

03:57.844 --> 04:01.871
Granted, we succeeded with those
tactics in the Oshima Bay battle.

04:02.081 --> 04:05.710
But the Bakan Straits are not only
narrow, the tides are far too swift to...

04:05.852 --> 04:07.615
...see well at night.

04:07.754 --> 04:10.780
There's a chance that we could
collide with a reef or an island.

04:11.991 --> 04:15.427
Besides, they've fallen to that strategy
once. Next time they'll be prepared.

04:15.595 --> 04:17.358
We need them to be
prepared for this to work.

04:18.398 --> 04:21.663
I only hope we get the
expected response from them...

04:22.635 --> 04:23.624
They'll respond.

04:23.736 --> 04:25.203
Sure they will!

04:25.738 --> 04:26.864
What do you think?

04:29.842 --> 04:31.833
All right, let's do it. Sakamoto!

04:45.425 --> 04:46.551
Get a move on!

04:46.726 --> 04:49.058
We're going to need all
the ammunition we've got!

05:04.477 --> 05:06.411
All right, load the guns!

05:06.512 --> 05:07.638
Prepare to fire!

05:07.747 --> 05:08.441
Yes, sir!

05:27.767 --> 05:28.927
Here we go!

05:29.869 --> 05:31.393
Fire!

05:43.149 --> 05:44.081
Admiral!

05:44.484 --> 05:46.543
We're under attack from
the Deshimura Battery!

05:47.086 --> 05:48.018
What the hell?

05:52.058 --> 05:54.788
Those cannons of theirs
can't reach us here.

05:54.961 --> 05:57.691
Damn, what a thorn in my side.

05:57.797 --> 06:00.265
Raise the anchor! Prepare for battle!

06:00.400 --> 06:03.028
But Admiral, in this darkness we won't...

06:03.302 --> 06:06.430
It doesn't matter, notify the
entire fleet to follow suit!

06:06.539 --> 06:07.005
Yes, sir!

06:14.580 --> 06:15.547
Here they come!

06:15.682 --> 06:17.809
Leading the fleet is the Fujiyamamaru!

06:18.117 --> 06:20.278
It's just as Sakamoto predicted.

06:20.386 --> 06:23.014
All right! Fire! Fire! Fire at will!

06:32.498 --> 06:33.726
Lights out!

06:33.866 --> 06:36.391
Turn right all the way!
Start advancing slowly!

06:49.015 --> 06:52.542
Drop anchor! Prepare to
fire from the port side!

06:54.921 --> 06:55.888
Move it!

07:00.259 --> 07:01.920
Fire all cannons!

07:09.268 --> 07:09.996
Damn!

07:10.303 --> 07:13.534
Commander Takasugi, there's no way
for us to take aim in this darkness!

07:16.375 --> 07:20.209
Forget about aiming, just fire away
in the direction of the cannonfire!

07:20.313 --> 07:21.007
Yes, sir!

07:27.887 --> 07:29.149
Bastards!

07:29.489 --> 07:31.753
Let them have it.
All the ammunition we've got!

07:42.268 --> 07:43.326
Are you all right?

07:43.436 --> 07:44.198
Yes, sir!

07:44.403 --> 07:46.997
But the thing is, we can't see a thing!

07:47.106 --> 07:49.040
Should we hold fire for now?

07:49.142 --> 07:49.870
No!

07:50.009 --> 07:53.445
Sakamoto told us to keep firing
until we're out of shot.

07:53.579 --> 07:55.376
We're not stopping!
Just keep blasting them!

07:55.481 --> 07:56.004
Yes, sir!

07:58.684 --> 07:59.981
Sakamoto!

08:06.759 --> 08:09.250
It's just as you predicted, Sakamoto.

08:10.897 --> 08:13.195
Think it's about time we jumped in?

08:13.332 --> 08:13.957
Yes.

08:14.634 --> 08:15.692
Prepare to set sail!

08:15.802 --> 08:16.928
Yes, sir!

08:18.004 --> 08:19.835
It would be hard enough by moonlight...

08:19.939 --> 08:21.964
...but do you think we'll
make it in this darkness?

08:22.108 --> 08:23.939
This is what we've been waiting for!

08:24.277 --> 08:26.074
The enemy's got a bigger ship.

08:26.179 --> 08:28.613
But our vessel's a
lot more maneuverable...

08:28.748 --> 08:31.911
...so when there's low
visibility, the advantage is ours!

08:32.251 --> 08:35.743
That's certainly true, but there's also
a chance that we could run aground.

08:35.888 --> 08:38.220
Sakamoto, can you really
see well enough to...

08:38.357 --> 08:40.382
...steer us safely
through this darkness?

08:40.660 --> 08:41.922
Cha, cha, cha!

08:42.061 --> 08:44.120
No, that's beyond me!

08:44.263 --> 08:47.357
But I have another set of eyes
that can see like an eagle!

08:48.067 --> 08:49.364
Another set of eyes?

08:59.045 --> 09:01.104
Admiral! We're being
swept away by the tide.

09:01.214 --> 09:04.012
At this rate, we won't be
able to continue our barrage.

09:04.984 --> 09:07.578
We chose the wrong spot to drop
anchor.

09:07.887 --> 09:08.945
Anchors aweigh!

09:09.388 --> 09:10.582
We're changing position.

09:10.690 --> 09:11.987
Don't let the tide sweep us!

09:12.124 --> 09:13.056
No, sir!

09:24.937 --> 09:26.370
Sakamoto!

09:49.862 --> 09:51.557
I can't see a thing out there!

09:52.331 --> 09:53.525
Are we gonna make it?

10:04.477 --> 10:06.240
Are we going to make it, Sakamoto?

10:06.812 --> 10:08.837
If for any reason we get
too close to the shore...

10:09.015 --> 10:10.949
...we might not be able
to avoid it in time.

10:11.350 --> 10:12.874
Should we use the engine?

10:13.019 --> 10:14.486
Stop worrying already!

10:14.587 --> 10:16.179
It won't do you any good.

10:16.489 --> 10:19.049
We have to be as silent as
possible, or they'll be onto us!

10:19.158 --> 10:21.149
Load the cannons on both sides!

10:47.653 --> 10:49.814
Ryoma, there's a rock
ahead, to the right.

10:50.389 --> 10:51.219
Go left!

10:51.357 --> 10:52.289
Hard aport!

11:00.499 --> 11:01.659
We're saved!

11:03.402 --> 11:05.029
There's a reef straight ahead!

11:06.238 --> 11:08.638
Where is it? I can't see a thing!

11:09.375 --> 11:13.277
Looks like we won't have time to
maneuver around that reef, Ryoma...

11:14.280 --> 11:16.077
Right, I know that.

11:16.215 --> 11:18.183
I'm leaving it all to you, Izumi!

11:33.399 --> 11:34.024
I see it!

11:34.133 --> 11:35.361
We're going to collide! Starboard!

11:35.501 --> 11:36.331
Keep going!

11:39.071 --> 11:40.197
Don't turn yet...

11:45.611 --> 11:47.135
Turn right, turn right, turn right!

11:49.882 --> 11:51.110
Now straighten out!

11:55.654 --> 11:57.315
Turn left 15 degrees!

12:06.065 --> 12:07.464
We made it through!

12:07.767 --> 12:08.825
We made it!

12:14.373 --> 12:15.931
I see...

12:16.108 --> 12:18.440
Instead of swerving to avoid the reef...

12:18.611 --> 12:22.012
...he got us through by cutting
it close in a straight line...

12:23.949 --> 12:25.473
You're amazing!

12:25.718 --> 12:27.310
I was sure we were going to crash!

12:27.486 --> 12:28.510
Quiet!

12:35.294 --> 12:36.886
Found them, Ryoma!

12:55.614 --> 12:57.309
Where are they? I can't see anything!

12:57.450 --> 12:58.246
They're to our right.

12:58.350 --> 12:59.442
Starboard!

12:59.585 --> 13:02.782
If we keep going like this,
which side will we pass them on?

13:03.155 --> 13:03.746
Right...

13:04.090 --> 13:05.352
Right, huh?

13:05.491 --> 13:06.958
That's perfect for us!

13:07.393 --> 13:09.122
Starboard, get ready to open fire!

13:09.328 --> 13:12.422
Stay on course! Let's slow down!

13:18.737 --> 13:19.669
An island!

13:19.805 --> 13:22.103
Sakamoto, we bore right too far!

13:22.341 --> 13:25.572
It's not an island,
it's the Fujiyamamaru!

13:27.746 --> 13:30.010
Izumi, you were right on the money!

13:32.918 --> 13:35.409
This is the best damned
warship in the country!

13:35.754 --> 13:37.187
We're out of your league!

13:37.523 --> 13:39.821
We'll show you how
powerful the Kaientai is!

13:48.868 --> 13:49.892
Enemy to the right!

13:50.269 --> 13:50.860
What?

13:56.108 --> 13:57.006
Fire!

14:05.851 --> 14:07.842
We've been struck on the starboard
side!

14:08.154 --> 14:09.348
The engine's been hit!

14:09.488 --> 14:11.115
We can't get any pressure up!

14:11.757 --> 14:14.123
But where the hell did
that ship come from?

14:14.226 --> 14:16.126
I didn't hear the engine!

14:19.465 --> 14:20.830
Hard aport!

14:20.966 --> 14:22.524
Take down the sails!

14:23.135 --> 14:26.866
Engine at full throttle, toss
in as much coal as we've got!

14:58.637 --> 15:00.195
The enemy's gaining on us!

15:00.439 --> 15:02.066
Full speed ahead!

15:02.208 --> 15:04.039
Starboard, prepare to
intercept enemy fire!

15:05.144 --> 15:06.805
Sneaking up on us in the darkness...

15:06.912 --> 15:09.403
...using their sails so
they won't make a sound...

15:09.648 --> 15:11.980
Then blasting their
cannons as they pass...

15:12.084 --> 15:15.019
Now they'll turn around and come
after us with their loaded side...

15:15.654 --> 15:18.987
Who in the hell is commanding that
ship?

15:34.707 --> 15:36.038
Take careful aim, now!

15:38.544 --> 15:39.203
Fire!

15:43.115 --> 15:45.242
Start blasting them as
soon as you're ready!

15:52.224 --> 15:53.657
Keep going parallel to them!

15:53.759 --> 15:55.488
Port side, don't stop firing!

16:11.143 --> 16:13.475
Why aren't we hitting them?

16:13.612 --> 16:16.706
Under these conditions, we
should be evenly matched...

16:17.549 --> 16:20.382
Granted, their vessel is
smaller and more maneuverable...

16:20.486 --> 16:24.252
Is it possible that they're actually
staying out of cannon range?

16:28.527 --> 16:30.654
No. 1 and No. 4?

16:30.796 --> 16:33.026
Gradually getting
shorter in between, I see...

16:34.099 --> 16:36.158
Ryoma, two more shots.

16:36.335 --> 16:38.929
Let's really outwit them
and keep moving forward!

16:39.171 --> 16:41.139
Right, I'm counting on you!

16:49.381 --> 16:50.405
An island!

16:50.616 --> 16:52.083
We're going to crash into Hikojima!

16:55.154 --> 16:58.089
Hard right! Retreat at full speed!

16:58.524 --> 17:00.151
Starboard!

17:08.801 --> 17:10.496
Too late, perhaps?

17:28.253 --> 17:30.118
Leak! We've sprung a leak!

17:40.733 --> 17:42.826
Surely they can't go on fighting now...

17:43.102 --> 17:44.034
Right.

17:44.203 --> 17:46.671
Let's move closer to their
starboard side, behind them...

17:56.081 --> 17:58.072
They're going for our blind spot...

17:58.183 --> 18:00.447
We can't possibly fire from there.

18:00.619 --> 18:02.348
Send the riflemen to the stern!

18:02.488 --> 18:03.045
Yes, sir!

18:09.061 --> 18:10.460
Look out, Sakamoto!

18:10.662 --> 18:12.152
All of you, go hide!

18:18.604 --> 18:19.730
Move it!

18:19.838 --> 18:20.827
Out of my way!

18:22.341 --> 18:23.399
Hold your fire!

18:23.675 --> 18:24.903
Everyone hold your fire!

18:26.178 --> 18:27.941
All right, listen up!

18:28.414 --> 18:31.247
I'm Ryoma Sakamoto of the Kaientai!

18:31.550 --> 18:33.177
Change is upon us!

18:33.452 --> 18:35.283
I, Ryoma, will see to
it that change comes!

18:36.955 --> 18:37.922
Give me that!

19:13.592 --> 19:15.082
The Bakufu is history.

19:15.194 --> 19:18.095
Nobody can stop its demise,
because it's destiny!

19:20.532 --> 19:21.521
Admiral!

19:21.900 --> 19:23.925
We can't stop the leaking!

19:24.169 --> 19:26.228
It's too much for our pumps to handle!

19:27.940 --> 19:28.907
Back off!

19:29.007 --> 19:29.871
Get out of here!

19:30.008 --> 19:31.999
If you die now it will be for nothing!

19:32.444 --> 19:35.971
Use those lives of
yours for the new Japan!

19:36.381 --> 19:38.178
We're heading for Kokura.

19:38.317 --> 19:39.443
Retreat at full speed!

19:46.191 --> 19:48.318
The Fujiyamamaru's fleeing!

20:00.105 --> 20:02.596
Sakamoto, it's the Bakufu fleet!

20:02.841 --> 20:05.241
Since it's almost time for daybreak...

20:05.377 --> 20:08.175
...they're sure to be able
to get a good look at us!

20:16.822 --> 20:18.312
It's Takasugi and his men!

20:19.791 --> 20:21.053
Fire!

20:31.203 --> 20:34.070
The Bakufu fleet is running away
with its tail between its legs!

20:34.172 --> 20:35.332
We did it!

20:36.542 --> 20:37.804
We won!

20:39.945 --> 20:43.745
The Bakufu no longer has the
power to sustain the nation.

20:44.449 --> 20:47.350
The Fujiyamamaru is a
mirror image of the Bakufu.

20:47.486 --> 20:49.454
Sure, it's huge, but
that's all there is to it.

20:49.655 --> 20:51.714
It has no intention of looking forward.

20:52.024 --> 20:56.188
And so a new age will come,
thanks to Ryoma Sakamoto...

20:56.328 --> 20:58.319
...who's always looking forward!

20:58.463 --> 20:59.191
Right?

21:01.133 --> 21:02.361
Cha, cha, cha!

21:03.669 --> 21:10.370
The following year, on October
15, 1867, the third year of Keio...

21:10.909 --> 21:14.811
...the Shogun finally abdicated,
and the Bakufu returned...

21:14.980 --> 21:17.471
...political power to the Emperor.

21:17.749 --> 21:20.718
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.363 --> 21:43.400
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at
them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:43.675 --> 21:53.414
<i>My loneliness and the vast night
sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.552 --> 22:02.551
<i>I just don't know what this
dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:02.694 --> 22:13.366
<i>Even if it's just "hello",
I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.406 --> 22:20.538
<i>The person I am today
is about to disappear...</i>

22:20.912 --> 22:23.904
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:24.783 --> 22:31.052
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.356 --> 22:36.851
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:51.977 --> 22:55.435
That's right, you're going to make the
Kaientai known all around the world!

22:55.547 --> 22:59.347
So long as I'm by your side,
you'll never be in danger!

23:00.018 --> 23:01.781
Next episode of Age of Chaos...

23:01.953 --> 23:03.716
<i>The Jigen Style Assassin</i>

23:03.822 --> 23:06.154
Pay close attention, and wait!
